Zuo is a Racket variant in the sense that program files start with `#lang`,
and the module path after `#lang` determines the parsing and expansion of
the file content.
That's how the `make`-like DSL is defined, and even the base Zuo language is
defined by layers of `#lang`s.
One of the early layers implements macros.

See (https://docs.racket-lang.org/zuo/).
